From f859e33d5f295aa519f7b4fe9cbf2e7748409ccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:46:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sx8-int8 stage 10: S-X8 on the int8 coopmat1 MMQ kernel
 (exact (d,m) remap, exact b sums, RED twin, role/min-n knobs, tests)

S-X8 strategies give step = u*{4,1,1,2} and rlo = lo + q*{0,0,3,1}, so every 32-block is exactly w = lo + u*L with
L in [0,252]; stored as L-128 int8 with d = u, m = lo + 128u on the Q4_1-shaped dm branch of mul_mmq_cm1 (CPU check on
7 real tensors: rel_fro <= 3.3e-7 vs dequantize_row_sx8). Activation sums for the min term are exact int sums from the
q8_1 tile, not the fp16 ds.y. GGML_ARIFI_SX8_CM1=0 = float arm, GGML_ARIFI_SX8_CM1_RED=1 = planted-error twin (m = lo),
GGML_ARIFI_SX8_CM1_ROLES / _MIN_N = per-role and width selectors with a stderr receipt per role. The cm1 shmem probe
now knows SX8, which is also why the scalar SX8 MMQ under coopmat never registered on RDNA3 (stage 9 op probe:
sx8-int8mmq rows bit-identical to float).

Lane: sx8-int8-stage10-2026-10-02
